%I A397795 #13 Oct 21 2026 16:57:58
%S A397795 0,1,8,40,88,8,104,56,40,16,2024,508
%N A397795 a(n) is the numerator of the maximum expected number of steps until a random walker falls into the sea when walking on the cells of an n-celled polyknight island.
%C A397795 This is the polyknight version of A366998.
%H A397795 Pontus von Brömssen, <a href="https://oeis.org/plot2a?name1=A397795&amp;name2=A397796&amp;tform1=untransformed&amp;tform2=untransformed&amp;shift=0&amp;radiop1=ratio&amp;drawpoints=true">Plot of a(n)/A397796(n) vs n</a>, using Plot2.
%H A397795 <a href="/index/Pol#polyominoes">Index entries for sequences related to polyominoes</a>.
%F A397795 For 1 <= n <= 9, the maximum expected number of steps is a(n)/A397796(n) = 8*(n+7)/(65-n). This is attained by a polyknight consisting of the starting square together with n-1 of the 8 squares reachable in a knight's move.
%Y A397795 Cf. A030446, A326954, A366998, A397796 (denominators).
%K A397795 nonn,frac,hard,more,changed
%O A397795 0,3
